"""Canned interpolation profiles (docs/design/ramps.md): firmware-side ramps of
uniforms and the FX crossfade toward a known endpoint, over a known duration,
with a known ease — evaluated once per frame per ramp on the device, so an agent
or the app sends ONE request instead of streaming steps.

no_std, zero-dependency, integer (Q16) ease math so the per-frame cost on the
C6 (no FPU) is a handful of integer ops per ramp plus one lerp per ramped float.
Driven by the render loop through the player FFI (//firmware/player_app:ffi.rs);
the keypoint morph (//firmware/keypoint) shares its eases and clock."""

load("@rules_rust//rust:defs.bzl", "rust_library", "rust_test")

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

rust_library(
    name = "ramp",
    srcs = ["src/lib.rs"],
    crate_name = "ledmapper_ramp",
    edition = "2021",
)

rust_test(
    name = "ramp_test",
    srcs = ["tests/ramp.rs"],
    edition = "2021",
    deps = [":ramp"],
)
